1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,400
Luke, 19.

2
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:06,140
He entered Jericho and was passing through.

3
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:08,780
And there was a man named Zacchaeus.

4
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:11,780
He was a chief tax collector and was rich.

5
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,960
And he was seeking to see who Jesus was,

6
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,920
but on account of the crowd he could not,

7
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,960
because he was small of stature.

8
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:23,420
So he ran on ahead and climbed up into a sycamore tree to see him,

9
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:25,620
for he was about to pass that way.

10
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:28,200
And when Jesus came to the place,

11
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:29,780
he looked up and said to him,

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,120
Zacchaeus, hurry and come down,

13
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:35,380
for I must stay at your house today.

14
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:39,060
So he hurried and came down and received him joyfully.

15
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:41,980
And when they saw it, they all grumbled.

16
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:45,440
He has gone in to be the guest of a man who was a sinner.

17
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:48,300
And Zacchaeus stood and said to the Lord,

18
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:52,400
Behold, Lord, the half of my goods I give to the poor,

19
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:55,120
and if I have defrauded anyone of anything,

20
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:56,940
I restore it fourfold.

21
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:58,800
And Jesus said to him,

22
00:00:59,620 --> 00:00:59,860
Today.

23
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,240
A salvation has come to this house,

24
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,620
since he also is a son of Abraham.

25
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:08,900
For the Son of Man came to seek and to save the lost.

26
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:10,860
As they heard these things,

27
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:13,960
he proceeded to tell a parable because he was near to Jerusalem,

28
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:18,540
and because they supposed that the kingdom of God was to appear immediately.

29
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:20,360
He said, therefore,

30
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:25,760
A nobleman went into a far country to receive for himself a kingdom and then return.

31
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:29,620
Calling ten of his servants, he gave them ten minas,

32
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,960
and said to them,

33
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:33,280
Engage in business until I come.

34
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:35,540
But his citizens hated him,

35
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,860
and sent a delegation after him, saying,

36
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:40,800
We do not want this man to reign over us.

37
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:43,840
When he returned, having received the kingdom,

38
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:46,820
he ordered these servants to whom he had given the money

39
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:48,180
to be called to him,

40
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:51,620
that he might know what they had gained by doing business.

41
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:54,700
The first came before him, saying,

42
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:57,880
Lord, your mina has made ten minas more.

43
00:01:58,380 --> 00:01:59,620
And he said to him,

44
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,620
Well done, good servant,

45
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:04,240
because you have been faithful in a very little.

46
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:07,280
You shall have authority over ten cities.

47
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:09,480
And the second came, saying,

48
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:12,300
Lord, your mina has made five minas.

49
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:13,740
And he said to him,

50
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:16,520
And you are to be over five cities.

51
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:18,600
Then another came, saying,

52
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:23,720
Lord, here is your mina, which I kept laid away in a handkerchief.

53
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:27,660
For I was afraid of you, because you are a severe man.

54
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:29,580
You take what you did not deserve,

55
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:32,220
deposit, and reap what you did not sow.

56
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,040
He said to him,

57
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:37,860
I will condemn you with your own words, you wicked servant.

58
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,880
You knew that I was a severe man,

59
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,640
taking what I did not deposit,

60
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:44,660
and reaping what I did not sow.

61
00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:48,280
Why then did you not put my money in the bank,

62
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:51,620
and at my coming I might have collected it with interest?

63
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:54,260
And he said to those who stood by,

64
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:56,100
Take the mina from him,

65
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:58,180
and give it to the one who has the ten minas.

66
00:02:58,700 --> 00:02:59,560
And they said to him,

67
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:02,380
Lord, he has ten minas.

68
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:06,320
I tell you that to everyone who has, more will be given.

69
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:08,220
But from the one who has not,

70
00:03:08,620 --> 00:03:10,520
even what he has will be taken away.

71
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,980
But as for these enemies of mine,

72
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,920
who did not want me to reign over them,

73
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:18,100
bring them here and slaughter them before me.

74
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:21,060
And when he had said these things,

75
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:23,320
he went on ahead going up to Jerusalem.

76
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:26,120
When he drew near to Bethphage and Bethany,

77
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:27,900
at the mount that is called Olivet,

78
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:29,540
he sent two of the disciples,

79
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:30,080
saying,

80
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:32,620
Go into the village in front of you,

81
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:34,940
where on entering you will find a colt tied,

82
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,280
on which no one has ever yet sat.

83
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:39,340
Untie it and bring it here.

84
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:41,260
If anyone asks you,

85
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:42,860
Why are you untying it?

86
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:44,220
You shall say this,

87
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,380
The Lord has need of it.

88
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,200
So those who were sent away

89
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:50,000
and found it just as he had told them.

90
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:52,360
And as they were untying the colt,

91
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:53,940
its owner said to them,

92
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:55,920
Why are you untying the colt?

93
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:57,400
And they said,

94
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:59,360
The Lord has need of it.

95
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:01,280
And they brought it to Jesus,

96
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:03,200
and throwing their cloaks on the colt,

97
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:04,800
they set Jesus on it.

98
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:06,440
And as he rode along,

99
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:08,120
they spread their cloaks on the road.

100
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:09,920
As he was drawing near,

101
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:12,560
already on the way down the Mount of Olives,

102
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:14,860
the whole multitude of his disciples

103
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:18,080
began to rejoice and praise God with a loud voice

104
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:21,120
for all the mighty works that they had seen, saying,

105
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:23,540
Blessed is the King

106
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:26,600
who comes in the name of the Lord.

107
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,400
Peace in heaven!

108
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,760
And glory in the highest!

109
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:35,180
And some of the Pharisees in the crowd said to him,

110
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:37,580
Teacher, rebuke your disciples.

111
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,200
He answered,

112
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,180
I tell you, if these were silent,

113
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:44,620
the very stones would cry out.

114
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:47,560
And when he drew near and saw the city,

115
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,240
he wept over it, saying,

116
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:52,080
Would that you, even you,

117
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,600
had known on this day

118
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,740
the things that make for peace!

119
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:58,780
But now they are hidden from your eyes.

120
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:01,520
For the days will come upon you

121
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:04,820
when your enemies will set up a barricade around you

122
00:05:04,820 --> 00:05:07,920
and surround you and hem you in on every side

123
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:10,820
and tear you down to the ground,

124
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:14,100
you and your children within you.

125
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:17,980
And they will not leave one stone upon another in you,

126
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:22,400
because you did not know the time of your visitation.

127
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:24,920
And he entered the temple

128
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:27,080
and began to drive out those who sold,

129
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:27,940
saying to them,

130
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:29,640
It is written,

131
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:32,420
My house shall be a house of prayer,

132
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:35,720
but you have made it a den of robbers.

133
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:38,380
And he was teaching daily in the temple.

134
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:41,300
The chief priests and the scribes

135
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:42,580
and the principal men of the people

136
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:44,260
were seeking to destroy him,

137
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:46,700
but they did not find anything they could do,

138
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:49,240
for all the people were hanging on his words.

